I traced the problem for some time and finally found that "-mieee"
in GCC 3 solved the mysterious crashes. Evidently I could not get
the older compiler to produce code that treated floating-point
arithmetics according to the IEEE standard.

> >> Do you know if this Deb kernel built with gcc 3 ?
> >
> >AFAIK, using GCC 3 for compiling the kernel is not (yet) supported nor
> >encouraged. I'm not even sure if it compiles without patching.
> 
> OK.  If gcc 3 is as much quicker for alpha as has been suggested, it 
> should be worth the wait !

One pointer against trying to compile the kernel with GCC 3 is that
the kernel is not hacked for that particular set of quirks and
incompatibilities. I'm under the impression that some new conventions
have been introduced with GCC 3. A quick look at Kernel Traffic gave
me this: http://kt.zork.net/kernel-traffic/kt20010730_128.html#8 .

