> What else can I try?

You can try hooking up a serial terminal (or PC with HyperTerm and the
like) on the first serial port. Switch it 9600,n,8,1 and see if you 
get some output when you power the board on.

Also be sure that the CPU fan is running and that the FAN has got a
three wire connector because the MB senses the FAN speed and won't
come up if the FAN speed is too low.

