and again i too think that you have to figure out the srm-devicenames first.
the command is :
sh dev
then if you know what your drive is (dka.. , dkb ...) you should check your
settings boot*:
sh boot*
if that does not work (old srm's do not support '*') try
1. sh boot_osflags
2. sh boot_defdev
3. sh auto_action
settings should be
1.A - for Multiusermode, S for Single-Usermode
2. device where your os is installed (dka100 for scsi-id 1 on
Channel/Controller 0)
3. A for Auto
i have to point out, that i do not have experience on linux on those alpha
boxes, but have installed DEC OSF/Tru64 many times on those types of
machines.

hope it helps



