Shot in the dark.  Some of the other TGA cards (ZLXp-E2 and -E3) came with
one of the color signal grounds (I think it was green) floating; the
original DEC cables apparently would tie it to the common signal reference
ground.  In my case (-E2) I got blurry and fuzzy text and color shadowing to
a Nokia 447W and a DEC VRC21.  I ended up soldering a small jumper wire on
the TGA card at the solder pads for the HD15 connector that tied the green
ground to the red and blue ones.  End of problem.

The only flatpanels we've used are Spectre's (no model, sorry) and they have
been very sensitive to cable and connector quality.  Having the green signal
float, and possibly having sync-on-green enabled (if in SRM, its an option)
might be giving your monitor the hiccups.

Note that I've never used a -E1 card and do not know if it has the same
grounding issue as the bigger cards.

Rich Jordan


