In comp.os.linux.alpha, I wrote:

>Anybody out there using Compaq's 'ccc' C compiler? It comes with a man
>page (/usr/man/man1/ccc.1) which looks broken. It uses some
>"rsml coding", contains references to:
>
>.so /usr/man/sml
>.so /usr/man/rsml
>
>which are symbolic links to *existing* files from 'ccc' package.
>Nevertheless, "man ccc" output contains, for example, only option
>descriptions visible. The option names are blank.

Solved. One of the filter commands used by 'man' to process the man page
refuses to process the above macros, reporting:

<standard input>:3: won't source 
  `/usr/lib/compaq/ccc-6.2.9.506-1/alpha-linux/man/sml'
   outside of `/usr/man' without -U flag

and similar for "rsml". Both files should be "hard"-copied to /usr/man
instead of just symbolic linking. Then it works fine.

This also might explain why (as somebody has reported) it is working
out-of-the-box in RH 5.2, provided the older versions of filters used by
'man' are less restrictive on the paths to macros.

Michal.

-- 
