Hi friends,

I'm running SuSE 7.1 Alpha Edition on my XP1000 (EV6, DP264, Tsunami) using 
kernel 2.2.18. Sound chip is an ESS1887 configured for kernel sound support 
(not ALSA, it's not working, though). The problem I'm facing is the 
decreasing playback speed that can be noticed even on very simple tasks 
like deiconifying or moving a window, that obviously should not require a 
lot of power from any component. Right after the action has been performed, 
playback simply returns to normal speed. Hardware monitor shows not a 
significant increase on CPU usage neither while playing sound nor while 
moving a window. Application speed is not influenced, everyhting except 
sound operates as exspected. Seems to be a driver problem because any sound 
app shows the same symtom and is true for MP3 and WAV format (others not 
tested). 

You can find a list of installed/used software below.

If you would recommend simply using another kernel like 2.4, I can tell you 
that it doesn't work with other essential components/drivers like tape 
drive or RIAD. I already tested it.

I'd appreciate any suggestion. 
Thanks,

Steve.

Important parameters and activated modules:
-------------------------------

